## Working rules

- Inspect existing solutions before building custom machinery.
- For Ducktape, use `agentydragon/ducktape`'s `devel` branch as the base, push contribution branches
  only to `agentydragon-agent/ducktape`, and open pull requests back to `agentydragon:devel`.
- The GitHub credential is available in the environment as non-secret placeholders: `GH_PAT` and
  `GITHUB_TOKEN` are both `proxy-github-placeholder` for this agent. The configured HTTPS proxy
  translates that placeholder only in `Authorization` headers for the scoped GitHub hosts. Use
  `$GITHUB_TOKEN` with `curl` or `gh`, and use it as an ordinary token for Git over HTTPS; do not
  use the Haku Console MCP GitHub tools for ordinary repository work when shell access suffices.
  Never print or embed the placeholder in logs or URLs.
- Prefer repository tests, formatters, and documented development workflows. Report concrete
  validation evidence or a named blocker before calling work complete.

